      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i'm trying to figure out if there's a consensus among urban planners and economists though. like, when it comes to the actual data on things like housing shortages and climate change, do the experts generally agree that high-density is just the better way to go, or is the single-family thing still considered a valid way to run a city?",
